   "id": "avodah_zarah.25a.18",
   "daf": "25a",
   "sentenceId": 17,
   "he": "לֹא תִּתְיַיחֵד אִשָּׁה עִמָּהֶם, בְּמַאי עָסְקִינַן? אִילֵימָא בְּחַד, דִּכְוָותַהּ גַּבֵּי יִשְׂרָאֵל מִי שְׁרֵי? וְהָתְנַן: ״לֹא יִתְיַיחֵד אִישׁ אֶחָד עִם שְׁתֵּי נָשִׁים״!",
   "en": "§ The mishna teaches that «a woman may not seclude herself with» gentiles. The Gemara asks: «What are we dealing with? If we say» that we are dealing with a woman who secludes herself «with one» gentile, «is» this «permitted in the corresponding» situation «involving a Jew? But didn’t we learn» in a mishna (Kiddushin 80b): «One man may not seclude himself» even «with two women?» It is certainly forbidden for one man to be secluded with one woman."
  }
 ],
